[2026-07-14] Phase 1 — fixed the day-one-broken user-facing flows
Files: frontend/src/lib/api.ts, frontend/src/app/page.tsx, frontend/src/app/drops/page.tsx, frontend/src/app/leaderboard/page.tsx, frontend/src/app/wishlist/page.tsx, frontend/src/app/orders/page.tsx, frontend/src/context/CartContext.tsx, frontend/src/components/CartDrawer.tsx, frontend/next.config.ts, frontend/public/grid.svg, frontend/public/placeholder.jpg, backend/core/views.py, backend/core/stripe_service.py
Decisions:
- api.ts baseURL is now normalized (strip trailing /api, default localhost:8000) and every call path carries its own /api/ — this ends the recurring regression where NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL with vs without the /api suffix broke one set of calls. drops/ and leaderboard/ were the two calls missing the prefix; both fixed
- Added unwrap<T>(res) to api.ts for the DRF {count,next,results} envelope; used on drops/leaderboard/wishlist/orders. drops and wishlist were previously calling .find/.map on the envelope object and crashing (swallowed by catch → blank pages). Left Feed's own pagination handling alone since it also needs `next`
- Multi-item cart checkout: StripeService.create_checkout_session now takes a list of items (one line item each); the view accepts item_ids[] (item_id still works for BuyButton), validates every item before creating anything, and writes one PENDING Order per item all keyed to session.id via bulk_create. Webhook handle_checkout_completion loops all orders for the session and is idempotent (skips already-PAID) — a replayed webhook awards nothing twice
- bulk_create bypasses the Order created-signal, so the (buggy, pre-payment) order-created emails already stop firing on this path — consistent with Phase 2 which removes them entirely
- Made "Shop Collection" genuinely work instead of just repointing a dead link: added ?drop= filter to ItemViewSet.get_queryset (Item.drops M2M) and had the homepage read ?drop= into the memoized feedFilters; drops link now goes to /?drop=<id>#feed
- Wrapped homepage feedFilters in useMemo to kill the object-literal-in-deps refetch loop (pulled forward from Phase 3 since I was editing those lines)
- Stripe success: /orders reads ?success=true, shows a confirmation banner, clears the cart, and strips the param so refresh is clean. Cart is cleared only on successful return, never on the checkout redirect — a cancelled payment keeps the cart intact
- Created /grid.svg (CSS bg pattern, 7 pages) and /placeholder.jpg (next/image fallback, generated 600x800 via Pillow) — both were 404s. Added **.run.app /media/** to next.config image allowlist; kept the (unused) localhost patterns for local dev
- Pulled forward from Phase 3 while restructuring stripe_service.py: deleted the dead create_payment_intent and retrieve_session methods
- Deferred to Phase 3 (they couple with the wishlist keep/delete decision): the no-op Save/Share buttons on items/[id] and the Edit pencil in ListingsTable

[2026-07-14] Phase 2 — data integrity & trust: PII, eco stats, pre-payment emails, honest AI
Files: backend/core/serializers.py, backend/core/views.py, backend/config/settings.py, backend/core/signals.py, backend/notifications/signals.py, backend/core/ai_service.py, backend/.env.example, .github/workflows/deploy-backend.yml, frontend/src/app/items/[id]/page.tsx (deleted backend/core/eco_service.py)
Decisions:
- PII leak closed: email is now an owner-gated SerializerMethodField on both UserSerializer and UserProfileSerializer — public list/retrieve/leaderboard return email=null; only the authenticated owner sees their own. me GET/PATCH still return the owner's email
- Set global DEFAULT_PERMISSION_CLASSES=IsAuthenticatedOrReadOnly. This alone would have broken the Stripe webhook (Stripe POSTs unauthenticated), so added explicit @permission_classes([AllowAny]) to stripe_webhook. Every other viewset already declared explicit permissions; UserViewSet (the only implicit-AllowAny one) now declares IsAuthenticatedOrReadOnly
- Eco stats now reflect reality: listing grants only the 50 listing points; items_sold_count + co2/water are credited to the SELLER on the PENDING→PAID transition (the real reuse event), buyer still gets 20 points + bought_count. Deleted eco_service.py — it was dead and its 10.0/700 constants contradicted the signals' 5.5/2700
- Order emails moved from order-created to the PAID transition (reusing _old_status from core.signals' pre_save) — buyers no longer get "Order Confirmed" before paying. Note bulk_create in Phase 1 already stopped the created-signal firing; this makes the intent explicit and correct for any future single .save() path
- AI honesty: analyze_image tags results mock:true/false and logs a warning (was print); item detail page shows a "Sample analysis — AI unavailable" banner when mock. emails.py already logged failures via logger.error, left as-is
- Pre-wired GEMINI_API_KEY + EMAIL_HOST_USER/PASSWORD + DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL into settings.py, .env.example, and the workflow env.yaml. Unset GitHub secrets expand to "" which is harmless (matches defaults → mock AI / no-op email). To activate: add the GitHub Secrets, zero code change. Caveat: when enabling email, set all three email secrets together — an empty DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL would override the settings default

[2026-07-14] Phase 5 — test suite (written before the cleanup phases) + one real bug it caught
Files: backend/requirements-dev.txt, backend/pytest.ini, backend/config/test_settings.py, backend/conftest.py, backend/core/tests/* (auth, items, eco_points, orders, notifications, permissions), backend/core/security.py, backend/core/views.py, frontend/src/app/items/[id]/page.tsx, .github/workflows/deploy-backend.yml (deleted backend/core/tests.py stub)
Decisions:
- 25 pytest tests via pytest-django on SQLite in-memory (config.test_settings: throttles neutralized to None so view-level 'register'/'login' scopes still resolve, MD5 hasher, dummy Stripe keys, local file storage). Test deps live in requirements-dev.txt — NOT in the prod image (keeps the Cloud Run image lean/free-tier)
- Stripe is monkeypatched (StripeService.create_checkout_session → fake session); the webhook idempotency test calls handle_checkout_completion twice and asserts no double eco points. Order emails are spied via notifications.signals to assert they fire on PAID, never on PENDING
- REAL BUG the suite caught: ItemViewSet had no object-level ownership check — any authenticated user could PATCH/DELETE anyone's item (IDOR). Added IsOwnerOrReadOnly (core/security.py) and applied it to ItemViewSet. As a side effect the analyze action (POST, no per-action perm) is now owner-only, which also protects the Gemini budget from arbitrary triggering — gated the "Run AI Analysis" button to the owner in the UI so non-owners don't hit a 403
- CI now runs a `test` job that `deploy` needs — a red suite blocks the deploy. chat/tests.py stub isn't collected (pytest python_files=test_*.py); left for Phase 3

[2026-07-14] Phase 3 — kill dead code (WebSockets → polling, backend + frontend cleanup)
Files (backend): deleted chat/consumers.py, chat/routing.py, notifications/consumers.py, notifications/routing.py, notifications/urls.py; config/asgi.py, config/settings.py, config/urls.py, notifications/signals.py, requirements.txt, core/views.py, core/serializers.py, core/admin.py, notifications/admin.py (new), create_superuser.py, + new __init__.py in notifications/ & core/management[/commands]
Files (frontend): deleted StripeCheckout.tsx, WishlistButton.tsx, app/chat/page.tsx, 5 boilerplate SVGs; NotificationBell.tsx, app/messages/page.tsx, CountdownTimer.tsx, UserDropdown.tsx, app/items/[id]/page.tsx, ListingsTable.tsx, package.json, and unused-import trims in drops/leaderboard
Decisions:
- WebSockets removed entirely (they never worked on WSGI Cloud Run): deleted both apps' consumers/routing, simplified asgi.py to plain Django ASGI, dropped CHANNEL_LAYERS + ASGI_APPLICATION + daphne (INSTALLED_APPS) + daphne/channels (requirements), and stripped the group_send blocks from notifications/signals. Real-time is now polling: NotificationBell polls every 30s (was fetch-once-on-mount — the badge never updated), messages polls the conversation list too; both pause on document.hidden
- Deduped the notifications route: dropped the `path('api/notifications/', include('notifications.urls'))` shadow and kept the router registration (consistent with every other resource); deleted notifications/urls.py. Same URL/behavior
- Replaced the `__import__` lambda health check with a real health_check view (core/views.py); removed the duplicate api_view import; swapped both traceback.print_exc() for logger.exception; removed the dead LikeSerializer; registered the 8 unregistered models in admin (+ new notifications/admin.py); added the 3 missing __init__.py (implicit-namespace-package fragility)
- Hardened two hardcoded-secret spots: create_superuser.py now reads DJANGO_SUPERUSER_* from env and never prints the password; the DB fallback DSN lost its `:password` literal
- Frontend: wired the two dead item-page buttons — Save toggles the wishlist (existing but unreachable feature), Share uses navigator.share/clipboard; added Orders + Wishlist to the user dropdown so both built-but-unlinked pages are reachable; deleted the now-redundant WishlistButton.tsx; removed the no-op Edit pencil (no edit route exists); dropped the never-imported @stripe/* deps and synced the lockfile; fixed CountdownTimer's dependency-less useEffect (was re-registering a timer every render) with a single interval keyed on targetDate + an onComplete ref
- Left as pre-existing, out-of-scope-for-dead-code: `any` types, next/image `<img>` warnings, and unused locals in files I didn't otherwise touch (login/register/closet/dashboard). Next 16 build doesn't fail on these, so they don't block deploy

[2026-07-14] Phase 4 — deploy & config hygiene (NOT pushed — awaiting approval)
Files: backend/Dockerfile, backend/config/settings.py, backend/requirements.txt, backend/core/migrations/0011_rename_*.py (new); deleted backend/Procfile, backend/railway.toml, backend/build.sh, backend/runtime.txt, backend/deploy_to_gcp.sh
Decisions:
- Dockerfile CMD now runs `python manage.py migrate --noinput` before `exec gunicorn`. Migrations are idempotent and, at min-instances 0, run only on cold start. Consequence: a deploy that carries a new migration applies it to the live Supabase DB automatically — this is exactly why the push/deploy needs explicit approval
- Reconciled the Django version: the venv AND the migration stamps were already 5.2.8 while requirements pinned 5.1.4 — prod was deploying a different version than dev tests. Bumped the pin to Django==5.2.8 (what the 25 tests actually validate). This surfaced a pending migration because 5.2 changed the auto index-naming algorithm; generated 0011 — a pure RenameIndex on ecopointshistory (ALTER INDEX ... RENAME, safe/fast). Deploying WILL apply this rename
- Deleted the four dead deploy targets (Procfile=Heroku, railway.toml=Railway, build.sh=Render, runtime.txt) and deploy_to_gcp.sh (duplicated the CI deploy, hardcoded the project id, and pushed the entire local .env — live Stripe/Cloudinary secrets — to Cloud Run). CI on push-to-main is the only deploy path now
- Removed the stale `*.onrender.com` CSRF origin (Render is gone) and the duplicate FRONTEND_URL definition

[2026-07-16] Full visual redesign kickoff — "Paper Editorial" — Phase 1 (foundation) + prod data cleanup
Files: frontend/src/app/globals.css, frontend/src/app/layout.tsx, frontend/src/app/{login,sell,messages,leaderboard}/page.tsx, frontend/src/components/{StatsCard,MessageInput,RippleText}.tsx, .claude/launch.json (new thriftgram-frontend dev-server entry). Prod DB: deleted 4 orphaned ItemImage rows (ids 1-4, user's own test items).
Decisions:
- Verified every audit claim directly (Read on globals.css, live getComputedStyle on the deployed site, grep counts) before planning — a prior in-session subagent summary was rejected by the user as unverified and redone properly. Confirmed live: body was rendering in Arial despite Geist being loaded (globals.css:184 override), and found two bugs the code audit alone missed: the homepage hero is a copyrighted Studio Ghibli/Totoro image, and the WaveGallery "signature" section rendered as a 720px empty void because 4 of its 6 images 404 from Cloudinary
- Root-caused the 404s via Cloudinary's own API (cloudinary.api.resources), not just curl: 4 ItemImage rows referenced files that were never actually stored on Cloudinary — orphaned DB records, not a code bug. Confirmed these were the user's own test listings (Btech/apple/new/Cloudinary) and got explicit approval before deleting (prod DB write, per the AGENTS.md no-prod-changes-without-approval rule — "fix all three" alone wasn't taken as covering a DB write)
- Design direction (user-approved): cool paper-white palette (#FBFBF9 canvas, #0B0B0C ink, #1A47E8 accent — every pairing WCAG-contrast-computed, not eyeballed), editorial serif (Fraunces) + grotesk (Geist, already loaded) typography, and a strict glass rule: dark-tinted glass only over photography/scrims, never over the bare paper canvas (max 3 glass surfaces/view)
- Token migration strategy: remap-don't-rename. Kept the existing Solarized variable NAMES (base-03 etc, 390+ usages) but changed their VALUES to the new neutral palette, so the entire app re-themed correctly with zero page-level changes the moment globals.css landed — verified live (bodyBg/bodyColor flipped to the new palette immediately). Semantic aliases (--ink/--paper/--surface/--line/--muted) layered on top for new code; old names retired once every call site migrates
- Fixed the shadow-scale bug: box-shadow strings were filed under --color-shadow-* (the COLOR namespace), so shadow-md/lg silently fell back to Tailwind's stock gray. Moved to --shadow-* (the real namespace) — verified via getComputedStyle that --shadow-md now returns real box-shadow values
- REAL BUG caught during Phase 1 verification, not by inspection: `@theme inline` only inlines --font-sans/--font-display into the Tailwind-generated utility classes (.font-sans, .font-display) — it does NOT emit them as standalone queryable CSS custom properties. My first fix, `body { font-family: var(--font-sans) }`, was silently invalid (verified via getComputedStyle showing Preflight's default stack instead of Geist) and would have been the exact same class of bug as the original Arial override. Fixed by referencing the raw next/font variables (--font-geist-sans, --font-fraunces) directly, which ARE present on <body> — confirmed body font now resolves to "Geist, Geist Fallback, ..." and a test .font-display element resolves to "Fraunces, Fraunces Fallback, ..." with the -0.03em tracking applied
- Purged all 8 token-immune hardcoded hex escapes (6× inline `#F7F1E3`, 2× framer-motion animate-prop literals in login.tsx) so they can't survive the redesign as beige artifacts; also fixed RippleText's stale base-03 fallback and its request for "Inter" (never loaded) to Fraunces (now loaded, self-corrects within a frame via the existing rAF loop so no fonts.ready wait was needed)
- Added a thriftgram-frontend entry to .claude/launch.json for browser-based verification (repo previously only had unrelated VectorShift entries)
- Deferred to Phase 3 (Navbar subtree): the two dead `animate-in fade-in zoom-in-95` classes in NotificationBell/UserDropdown — fixing needs component JSX changes those files get anyway when restyled, so not worth a second pass
- Deferred to Phase 4 (signature moments, now unblocked): hero image replacement (typographic hero, no photo — user chose this over sourcing/using screenshot-quality product photos) and the WaveGallery rebuild (drop grayscale(1) brightness(0.5), fix the leaked global --index, fix the ≤480px wrap)
